questions.scenario:
You are debugging a production issue where an order processing system calls an external payment service via a child transactional bean. You observe that when `ExternalPaymentClient.charge()` fails with a `PaymentFailedException` (a `RuntimeException`), the catch block in `OrderService` attempts to record a failure status using `OrderRepository.save()`. However, the transaction ultimately fails at commit time, throwing `UnexpectedRollbackException`, and the failure log is never persisted.

java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    @Autowired private OrderRepository orderRepo;
    @Autowired private ExternalPaymentClient paymentClient;

    @Transactional
    public void processOrder(OrderRequest request) {
        try {
            paymentClient.charge(request); // @Transactional(propagation = Propagation.REQUIRED)
        } catch (Exception e) {
            // Attempting to record failure state
            orderRepo.save(new OrderLog(request.getId(), "FAILED"));
        }
    }
}
